    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d880">

                <pb facs="0965" n="953" sameAs="frus:frus1944v03/pg953"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 EW/1–245: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-01-02">January 2,
                        1945</date>.<lb/>[Received January 2—8:49 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6. Moscow papers January 2 announce delegation of Provisional Hungarian
                    Government has arrived in Moscow for armistice negotiations. It consists of
                    János Gyondesy [<hi rendition="#italic">Gyöngyösy</hi>] Minister of Foreign
                    Affairs and President of Delegation; Colonel General János Vörös; and Istvan
                    Balog, Secretary of State.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Caserta as 1.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
